{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-2732","published":"2026-06-24T11:11:39Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:21:11.219369514Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-49261"],"summary":"mariadb security update","details":"MariaDB is a community developed fork from MySQL - a multi-user, multi-threaded SQL database server. It is a client/server implementation consisting of a server daemon (mariadbd) and many different client programs and libraries. The base package contains the standard MariaDB/MySQL client programs and utilities.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nMariaDB server is a community developed fork of MySQL server. Versions 10.6.1 through 10.6.26, 10.11.1 through 10.11.17, 11.4.1 through 11.4.11, 11.8.1 through 11.8.7, and 12.3.1 with  `wsrep_notify_cmd` enabled would execute shell commands embedded in the name of the joiner node. This is fixed in 10.6.27, 10.11.18, 11.4.12, 11.8.8, and 12.3.2. As a workaround, anyone who cannot upgrade now should disable `wsrep_notify_cmd`.(CVE-2026-49261)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"mariadb","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/mariadb&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["mariadb-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-backup-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-common-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-config-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-debuginfo-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-debugsource-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-devel-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-embedded-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-embedded-devel-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-errmsg-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-gssapi-server-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-oqgraph-engine-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-pam-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-rocksdb-engine-10.5.29-5.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","mariadb-server-10.5